Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||08-02-2000||03:30 PM||||<BR>I have a 4 speed 84 Fiero SE, I just Ported the Head and TBI and instaled a Holley 300 TBI unit it also has a Stright through exhaust w/ side out tip, 1.6 roller rockers and wepapon R carbon intake w/ ram air, I started the car today for the first time with all the mods instaled the cars idle was 3000 rpm. I shut it off and checked for vac. leaks I found a leak @ the intake & TBI unit, With that fixed I Started her up again this time is revs up to 3000 RPM and drops to 2000 RPM and repeats over and over as the car warms up the RPM's drop off until it stals. Could this be my Map sensor? I have removed the Cruise Control system and pluged the vac. line could that be it? Pease help my Haynes book says nothing about this problem.||||reg||8
Z||000001||86SE||08-02-2000||03:42 PM||||Usually if its the MAP sensor, it will start up idle about normal, then the service engine light will come on and the revs will go way up.  Does your engine light come on?<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||08-02-2000||03:50 PM||||When the car first starts it will go straight to 3000 RPM and just keep reving up & down from 2000-3000 RPM as it warms up the car will rev from about 1000-2000 RPM and then stall out i have to tap the gas to keep it runing till it can cool down. the engine light is on.||||reg||1
