Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||08-02-2000||04:49 PM||||Is there any way to test the IAC, MAP and O2 sensors? Are they sensors I can use off of my parts cars?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||EdsB52||08-02-2000||05:12 PM||||Since you have the 4 banger, poor performance is an attribute that they're engineered to have. No but really, sounds like the IAC valve to me. It doesn't reset itself until 40mph. I would artificially plug the passage for a test run. It might run very rich for a moment, but that might eliminate one variable.||||reg||1
Z||000007||vinnywolfe||08-02-2000||07:06 PM||||i would almost bet it is your idle air control motor.  not sure how much they are new, but my guess is that since a stepper motor, it may be a little pricey.  for a few bucks, you could take several from a junk yard.  you're bound to have ONE that is good.<BR>but that's me and i'm a CHEAPSKATE.<BR>before you put the new one on, make sure you use a GOOD carb/throttle body cleaner ( i like the valvoline syntec stuff) and clean all around in the air passages, especially the area where the pintle valve on the iac comes in contact with the passage.<BR>i had a similiar problem on my 84 sc, and this cleared my idle right up.<P>vinny (87gt)<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000008||LarryB||08-02-2000||10:47 PM||||You say the engine light comes on, what are the codes being set?  The 3000RPM idling when cold and then dropping in steps sounds like:<P>the IAC is retracting properly when the engine is cold causing the high RPMS<P>when the ECM goes into closed loop mode and starts looking at the sensor info it adjusts the IAC to drop the idle but its either getting bad data or it can't properly compensate for a problem.  <P>My guess is you'd see a code 35 with maybe a TPS or O2 sensor-related error. <P>Problem could be the IAC, the MAP sensor, EGR, a vacuum leak, a fuel pressure problem, or maybe a connector to one of the sensors went bad.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Xtreme Fiero's||08-03-2000||12:09 AM||||The car never holds a steady Idle, It will rev itself in a 1000 RPM range and drop the range in steps usualy from 3000 to 2000 RPM, as the engine warms up is sounds like the engine has a load on it and is boging down. I can't give the  car a little gas to hold the RPM's above what it thinks is IDLE Because with My Mods the throttle response is so crisp and fast if I tap the gas the car will hit red line istantly. I am starting to think maby my mods are causing the problem I have included a compleet list of all my mods if any body can see a problem please let me know.<P>New parts:<BR>Holly 300 TBI<BR>Weapon R Carbon intake<BR>Crane 1.6 roller rockers<BR>Custom Ram Air<BR>DC Sports free flow exhaust<P>mods from before<BR>Saleen 10.4mm Wires<BR>NO Thermostat<BR>Holly Valve cover<BR>Accell coil & cap<BR>NKG plugs<BR>Ported Intake<BR>Ported Head<BR>Ported Header<BR>Dual Oil coolers w/ 900 cfm fans (under 85GT hood vents)<P> I hope this is not going to cost much to fix I have just replaced The IAC valve tonight I will see if it helped in the morning its way to loud t start now I'll wake up all of the east coast||||reg||4
